The source includes build scripts and third-party submodules. Bundled system
libraries retain their respective licenses and notices.

The task's installer extracts the AppImage without FUSE, replaces the Lua
startup script with an empty script and removes bundled Lua scripts. Product
binaries, libraries and image processing modules are unmodified. The Python
launcher sets instance directories, first-run defaults, CPU thread limits
and required Landlock filesystem/execution confinement. It requires enabled
Landlock ABI 1 or newer and uses the filesystem rights supported by that ABI.
File writes, creation and removal are restricted to the configured instance
directories and the required /dev/null and /dev/shm paths. Execution is limited
to the packaged application tree, /usr/bin/locale and the dynamic loader.
ABI 1 denies cross-directory renames and hard links. On ABI 2 or newer, these
operations are permitted only where the applicable Landlock path rules allow
them. File truncation is restricted only on ABI 3 or newer; the launcher
provides no truncation restriction on ABI 1 or 2. These task adapters are not
part of upstream darktable.
